{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/TrackingOpenSource"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Change a screen’s behavior based on how it came to be visible, with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" only model what a screen is showing right now — Empty, Loading, Data, or Error. They don’t know, and don’t need to know, how the screen got there. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource"},{"type":"text","text":" is a separate, independent type for exactly that: was the screen freshly pushed, revealed by popping something off a navigation stack, presented modally, opened from a deep link, or launched from a Home Screen shortcut?"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates can’t detect any of this on its own — there’s no "},{"code":"NavigationStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier or UIKit push interception behind "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource"},{"type":"text","text":". Your app already knows the answer wherever navigation actually happens (a coordinator, a router, a "},{"code":"NavigationStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" path change, "},{"code":"onOpenURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a shortcut-item handler), so it passes the value in explicitly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-concrete-example","text":"A concrete example","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The most common reason to care about this: skip a reload when the user is merely returning to a screen that’s already showing data, but do reload on a fresh push."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum AppScreen {","    case home, articleList, articleDetail","}","","@MainActor","final class ArticleListViewModel {","    let store = ScreenStateStore<[Article]>()","","    func onAppear(source: ScreenOpenSource<AppScreen>) {","        if source.isPop {","            return \/\/ already have data from before — nothing to do","        }","        Task { await store.loadCollection { try await api.fetchArticles() } }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"source.originatingScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives you the "},{"code":"Screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that triggered a "},{"code":".push","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".pop","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":".presented","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — useful for anything more specific than “was this a pop”, like varying copy or analytics by referrer:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["if source.originatingScreen == .home {","    \/\/ came straight from the home screen","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/trackingopensource"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource"],"title":"